In Go, modules enable us to manage dependencies and to represent one versioned unit of Go code.

A module file will be named go.mod and will look like this:

module projectnamehere.domainnamehere.com/net

go version x.xx.x

for example:

module myfishingblog.ariellarin.com

go version 1.27.0

require github.com/someone/coollibrarythatiwanttouse v1.4.2

Notice that last bit is a dependency that we are using. We can use other modules in our
own projects and specify the version that we want to use.